WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.935 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We are here celebrating
Thanksgiving with my family.

00:00:01.935 --> 00:00:06.473
And so far our older boy, Ashe,
has been very sweet to Axel.

00:00:06.473 --> 00:00:10.176
But you found an old baby book
where you filled in information.

00:00:10.176 --> 00:00:12.145 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what did you --
did you remember?

00:00:12.145 --> 00:00:14.514 size:81% position:41%
How did I treat Josh
when we were that age?

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:18.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You were not quite as loving,
I don't think.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:19.619 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You were beloved.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.887 line:92%
You were the sweetest boy.

00:00:20.887 --> 00:00:23.623 align:start size:94% position:6%
And poor Poshy
had a bad stomach situation,

00:00:23.623 --> 00:00:27.160 align:start size:94% position:6%
so he was kind of fussy
and not as --

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.461 line:92%
Yeah, he was a harder baby.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:31.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I think everybody could
tell that tonight.

00:00:31.064 --> 00:00:32.532 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:33.600 line:92%
-But anyhow, there was once

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:35.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember writing in
the baby book --

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:37.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
you must have been
about 2 1/2 --

00:00:37.370 --> 00:00:42.776
and you said, "Just leave Poshy
in his crib today

00:00:42.776 --> 00:00:45.845 line:92%
because he'll be just fine."

00:00:45.845 --> 00:00:47.313 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Is that your memory of it
as well?

00:00:47.313 --> 00:00:51.985
-I remember that he'd be playing
on the floor and you would --

00:00:51.985 --> 00:00:57.357
You know how like a dog can step
over things and never trips?

00:00:57.357 --> 00:00:58.491 line:92%
You could do the same thing.

00:00:58.491 --> 00:01:01.961 align:start size:94% position:6%
You would you step over Josh
as if he wasn't there.

00:01:01.961 --> 00:01:03.430 line:92%
But you never tripped over him,

00:01:03.430 --> 00:01:06.433 size:88% position:44%
but you just pretty much
ignored his existence.

00:01:06.433 --> 00:01:09.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I was elusive.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.135 --> 00:01:11.838 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Like a ninja.
-Yeah.

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:12.972 line:92%
-You guys figured something out.

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:15.608 align:start size:94% position:6%
I knew that Josh and I are
about two years apart.

00:01:15.608 --> 00:01:17.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
And Ashe and Axel
are about two years apart.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:20.013
But you guys figured out
something pretty amazing.

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:24.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's exactly two year--
yeah, the distance --

00:01:24.651 --> 00:01:26.186 size:84% position:42%
-Two years and 11 days.
-Two years and 11 days.

00:01:26.186 --> 00:01:28.521 align:start size:94% position:6%
-For both Josh and I
and my two boys,

00:01:28.521 --> 00:01:30.156 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is
a fantastic coincidence.

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:33.726
-I always said two years
was the perfect difference.

00:01:33.726 --> 00:01:34.294 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-And 11 days.

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:35.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And 11 days.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:38.264
-You end up on the other side of
that 11 days, yeah.

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:42.535
You do not -- We post a lot of
photos of our kids, obviously,

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:43.603 line:92%
like a lot of parents do.

00:01:43.603 --> 00:01:46.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's easier than ever now
with photo sharing.

00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:49.709
There's one kind of photo of
children you do not care for.

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:53.379 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't like food
on those kids' faces.

00:01:53.379 --> 00:01:53.913 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I don't like it.

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:57.183
I don't like it if kids are
outside playing in the dirt.

00:01:57.183 --> 00:01:57.851 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
That's great.

00:01:57.851 --> 00:01:59.252 size:78% position:39% line:92%
But, like, covered --

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:03.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
Also your kids have a lot of,
like, green smoothies.

00:02:03.890 --> 00:02:05.191 line:92%
They're keeping it healthy.

00:02:05.191 --> 00:02:08.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it just looks gross.
I don't like it.

00:02:08.328 --> 00:02:09.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
Like, they're cute kids.
I love them.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:12.732
And I don't like it when they
got stuff all over their face.

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:15.568 size:75% position:38%
And I know you have,
like, rags around.

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:17.137 line:92%
I know you have wet ones.

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:20.573 line:92%
-We have the finest rags.

00:02:20.573 --> 00:02:23.510 size:88% position:44% line:92%
We have Egyptian cotton.

00:02:23.510 --> 00:02:25.845 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
No, I love pictures of them,

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.981 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they got stuff
on their faces.

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:31.284 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And the other thing I noticed
that's happened recently

00:02:31.284 --> 00:02:34.621
is when we were walking down
the street about a month ago

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:38.391
and you had Axel in front of you
in a carrier,

00:02:38.391 --> 00:02:41.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
and these people
were coming toward us.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:45.231 align:start size:94% position:6%
Somebody goes,
"Hey, that's Seth Meyers."

00:02:45.231 --> 00:02:49.002
And the other person said,
"And that's the lobby baby."

00:02:49.002 --> 00:02:50.703 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.703 --> 00:02:53.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
So they're infamous.
-Yeah. He's a lobby baby now.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:54.274 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-He's a lobby baby.

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:57.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's a good way
of living his life, man, yeah.

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.244 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I just hope he --

00:02:58.244 --> 00:03:00.880
You know, he should try to
always look like he does now,

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:03.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
'cause otherwise people are
gonna forget it was him, yeah.

00:03:03.783 --> 00:03:04.250 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-True.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.487
-We talked a lot about what you
wanted the kids to call you

00:03:07.487 --> 00:03:09.088 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you first
became grandparents.

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your original plan was
you wanted to be called...

00:03:11.925 --> 00:03:13.359 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Cisco.
-Cisco.

00:03:13.359 --> 00:03:15.862 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:15.862 --> 00:03:17.597 line:92%
And you wanted to be called...?

00:03:17.597 --> 00:03:20.266 line:92%
-I toyed with a bunch of ones,

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:25.572 align:start size:94% position:6%
like my grandmother was Nani,
the Swedish one.

00:03:25.572 --> 00:03:27.740
But I didn't really know.
-You didn't really know.

00:03:27.740 --> 00:03:32.579
And what happened was we all,
my brother and I, Josh and I,

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:34.814 line:92%
still call you Hurry and Yarry,

00:03:34.814 --> 00:03:37.917
which were nonsense names
we've called you our whole life.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:38.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Right.
-Right.

00:03:38.651 --> 00:03:41.454 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Which were the nonsense names
you guys called each other

00:03:41.454 --> 00:03:42.589 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
when you met.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:44.457 size:78% position:39%
-Not when we met, no.
-Not the first day.

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:47.794
-No, he was putting moves on me
then.

00:03:47.794 --> 00:03:49.262 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-"Hey, Hurry!"

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.129 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.564 size:78% position:39% line:92%
"How you feel, girl?"

00:03:51.564 --> 00:03:53.233 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.233 --> 00:03:55.268 line:92%
Snapped her up like that.

00:03:55.268 --> 00:03:59.439 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.439 --> 00:04:02.141 size:78% position:39%
-Your pickup line was
to call her Hurry.

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:05.645 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Never worked before.
-Yeah.

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:09.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's what he calls you,
is Hurry and Yarry.

00:04:09.148 --> 00:04:10.483 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Yeah, but they -- Paca.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:12.318 line:92%
He puts the "paca" in front.

00:04:12.318 --> 00:04:13.253 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-Yeah, he thought --

00:04:13.253 --> 00:04:15.488 align:start size:94% position:6%
For whatever reason
Grandpa was Paca.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:16.889 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, you're Paca Hurry
and Paca Yarry,

00:04:16.889 --> 00:04:19.993
so I feel like when they hear
him talking to you in the park,

00:04:19.993 --> 00:04:23.730
they think he's from some weird
Eastern European country.

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:24.597 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.597 --> 00:04:26.633 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Paca Hurry!"
-Yeah.

00:04:26.633 --> 00:04:27.200 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:30.036 align:start size:94% position:6%
-"Paca Yarry, can we have
iced cream?"

00:04:30.036 --> 00:04:33.306 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, no, you don't know
Paca Alexi.

00:04:33.306 --> 00:04:35.174 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

